p and clear diagram reasoning.","explain":"Year 7 students develop measurement problem solving with explicit methods, worked numerical examples and reasonableness checks. Represent the situation, choose an appropriate procedure, calculate carefully and verify with an inverse, estimate or diagram. Catalogue alignment uses MA4-ARE-C-01; detailed content-point mapping remains pending.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Using parallelogram area for triangles without 1/2, or assuming all shapes have the same angle sum. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Measurement problem solving.","caption":"Then check.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Represent</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">diagram/expression</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Calculate</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">careful steps</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the p